  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Magellan Federal has $287M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 33 awards, with an average award size of $8.7M. Obligations fell 20.5% year over year. Magellan Federal’s FY2026 obligations concentrate in a few places: the General Services Administration obligated $189M, the Department of the Interior obligated $45.8M, and the Department of Defense obligated $29.8M. Magellan Federal’s largest markets are Other Individual and Family Services at $215M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $52.7M. Historical obligations show variability, with FY21 at $212M, FY22 at $249M, FY23 at $400M, FY24 at $334M, FY25 at $360M, and FY26 at $287M. Smaller FY2026 obligations include the Department of Transportation at $1.5M, the Department of Health and Human Services at $20.5M, and nominal amounts such as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission at $46.4K and the Department of Justice at $16K. The FY2026 mix reflects services-focused work, with Human Resources Consulting Services at $11.4M and Engineering Services at $6.4M among the listed NAICS markets.",
    "sections": [
